WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.331
AWS shipped a free local

00:00:02.131 --> 00:00:04.032
AWS for your laptop,

00:00:03.832 --> 00:00:05.555
and no human wrote or

00:00:05.355 --> 00:00:06.898
reviewed its code.

00:00:07.598 --> 00:00:09.202
That is the project lead.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.841
AWS Emulator came out November

00:00:11.641 --> 00:00:14.332
eleventh, and AWS says agents

00:00:14.132 --> 00:00:15.440
wrote all of it.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.803
It answers AWS calls on

00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:18.992
a local port,

00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:20.691
so your tools and agents

00:00:20.491 --> 00:00:22.389
can test with no account

00:00:22.189 --> 00:00:23.154
and no bill.

00:00:23.704 --> 00:00:25.638
Launch coverage says over two

00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:26.679
hundred services.

00:00:26.719 --> 00:00:28.735
Calls it cannot handle return

00:00:28.535 --> 00:00:29.970
error five oh one,

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:31.132
so gaps fail loudly.

00:00:31.682 --> 00:00:33.900
Install it, unset your real

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.434
AWS keys so tests never

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.968
touch your account,

00:00:36.768 --> 00:00:38.582
then add the agent skill.

00:00:39.132 --> 00:00:40.126
The catch:

00:00:39.926 --> 00:00:41.929
it does not check permissions

00:00:41.729 --> 00:00:43.084
the way AWS does,

00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:44.454
so a call your account

00:00:44.254 --> 00:00:45.753
would refuse can pass.

00:00:45.793 --> 00:00:46.939
Do not use it for

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:48.031
security testing.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.304
Three agent teams built it.

00:00:50.344 --> 00:00:52.696
Test writers check real AWS,

00:00:52.496 --> 00:00:55.095
issue finders file mismatches,

00:00:54.895 --> 00:00:57.164
and fixers take one issue each.

00:00:57.714 --> 00:00:59.761
Every change must compile,

00:00:59.561 --> 00:01:01.092
pass agent review,

00:01:00.892 --> 00:01:03.161
survive security agents and keep

00:01:02.961 --> 00:01:04.196
fidelity scores.

00:01:04.236 --> 00:01:05.991
Fail once, and it goes back.

00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:07.820
If this holds up,

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.778
senior engineers read fewer diffs

00:01:09.578 --> 00:01:10.925
and own the specs,

00:01:10.725 --> 00:01:12.612
the tests and the gate instead.

00:01:13.162 --> 00:01:14.998
Setup steps and every limit

00:01:14.798 --> 00:01:16.208
are in the full story

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.133
on The Dispatch.

